Article 5 (Standards for Scholarship Payments)
Scholarships shall be paid in accordance with the following standards: <Amended on May 8, 1979.>
1. For middle-school students, special emphasis shall be placed on persons who intend to major in natural science or technology in the future;
2. For high-school students, recipients receiving vocational education or technical education shall account for at least 60 percent of all persons selected for payment;
3. For university students, persons majoring in natural science or technology shall account for at least 70 percent of all persons selected for payment;
4. For graduate students, priority shall be given in particular to persons selected as prospective teaching personnel or researchers in the natural sciences;
5. For researchers, persons conducting research in natural science or technology shall account for at least 80 percent of all persons selected for payment.
